title: Party Agenda
subtitle: Work of the party that shapes its character.
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: {! return !!Q.S && !!Q.polish_party_rules && PolishParty.agendaAvailable(Q) !}
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
// The party's standing actions (technical reference 4.4, 13.1–13.2, 17.2; card catalogue 5.5–5.9): each costs this
// month's action; organisational work needs no money. Since Z — 0.57 (item 11 of the play notes of 5 X 2026) it is an
// ordinary card of the Party deck, no longer pinned: it has to be drawn and goes back to the hand unused. Z — 0.78 (decision 5A
// of 8 X 2026): the TUR courses have their own card, polish_party_tur. Z — 0.92: the cooperative is founded on the card
// Organisations of PPS at once. Z — 1.19 (decisions 1A, 2B, 3A and 4A of 22 XI 2026): six kinds of work, each building a
// characteristic of the party; the extraordinary collection and the steps of the agreement with the KPP left the card, and
// the dues bring money every month.
PolishParty.agendaView(Q);
// Stage 7: the assessment of the forces of the state was a standing action of this agenda; Z — 1.08 (decision 7A) removed it.
!}

= The party agenda

Party money: [+ pl_pa_cash_words +]. The dues bring [+ pl_pa_dues_monthly +] every month.

TUR: [+ pl_party_tur +].

[? if pl_pa_priorities : Economic priorities of PPS: [+ pl_pa_priorities +]. Each is prepared through its government card, with its own costs. ?]

- @organize_unions
- @organize_rural
- @organize_minorities
- @organize_councils
- @organize_rallies
- @kpp_work
- @easy_discard

@organize_unions
title: Work in the unions
subtitle: Cost: 0 resources. The activists strengthen all three unions at once. Builds unionism.
choose-if: {! return PolishParty.agendaWorkStatus(Q, 'unions').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_pa_work_unions_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.agendaWork(Q, 'unions');
!}
go-to: result

@organize_rural
title: Work in the villages
subtitle: Cost: 0 resources. The activists reach the peasants and the farm workers. Builds the worker-peasant alliance.
choose-if: {! return PolishParty.agendaWorkStatus(Q, 'rural').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_pa_work_rural_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.agendaWork(Q, 'rural');
!}
go-to: result

@organize_minorities
title: Work among the minorities
subtitle: Cost: 0 resources. The activists reach the voters of the national minorities. Builds federalism.
choose-if: {! return PolishParty.agendaWorkStatus(Q, 'minorities').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_pa_work_minorities_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.agendaWork(Q, 'minorities');
!}
go-to: result

@organize_councils
title: Work in the town councils
subtitle: Cost: 0 resources. The councillors of PPS deal with the everyday matters of the towns, which the workers and the intelligentsia notice. Builds reformism and parliamentarism.
choose-if: {! return PolishParty.agendaWorkStatus(Q, 'councils').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_pa_work_councils_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.agendaWork(Q, 'councils');
!}
go-to: result

@organize_rallies
title: Rallies in the factories
subtitle: Cost: 0 resources. The speakers of the party address the workers, who become more ready to strike. Builds strike action.
choose-if: {! return PolishParty.agendaWorkStatus(Q, 'rallies').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_pa_work_rallies_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.agendaWork(Q, 'rallies');
!}
go-to: result

@kpp_work
title: Cooperation with the communists
subtitle: Cost: 0 resources. Improves our relations with the KPP, which are [+ kpp_relation : relationships +] today, but displeases the Centre of the party. Good relations open the cabinets of the left with the communists. Builds radicalism.
choose-if: {! return PolishParty.agendaWorkStatus(Q, 'kpp').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_pa_work_kpp_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.agendaWork(Q, 'kpp');
!}
go-to: result

@result
new-page: true

= The party agenda

[+ pl_party_result +]

- @root: Continue.
